WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.980
- Do you remember when they
first asked you to host?

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:02.813
- Oh, yeah.

00:00:02.813 --> 00:00:03.660
- 'Cause it was such
a random thing, right?

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:05.130
- Well, yes.

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:08.250
They asked me to host and
they didn't know what.

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:10.080
Everybody was flying blind the first year,

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.270
including me, 'cause I had
never been to a dog show,

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:13.890
I didn't no know anything about 'em.

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:15.660
They brought the Old English Sheepdog

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.010
up to the judge.
- Oh, yeah.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:19.610
- If you don't know what
an Old English Sheepdog is,

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:23.670
it's 80 pounds of hair and
two pounds of actual dog.

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:24.503
- [Kelly] Yeah.
(audience laughs)

00:00:24.503 --> 00:00:25.620
Which is awesome!
- So, they brought it up

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:28.080
to the judge who was this
elegantly gowned woman.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:29.880
So she walks around to
the front of the dog

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:31.500
and she starts picking
through all of the hair

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:32.737
on the dog's head, and I said,

00:00:32.737 --> 00:00:34.170
"David, what is she doing now?"

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:36.781
He says, "John, she's
trying to find the eyes

00:00:36.781 --> 00:00:37.614
(audience laughs)

00:00:37.614 --> 00:00:39.630
"to gauge the attentiveness of the dog."

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:40.463
I said, "Really?"

00:00:40.463 --> 00:00:41.707
I said, "Well if she picks
through all of that hair

00:00:41.707 --> 00:00:42.817
"and she finds only one eye,

00:00:42.817 --> 00:00:44.322
"she's got the wrong end of the dog."

00:00:44.322 --> 00:00:46.620
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:49.119
So you see how far my learning curve was?

00:00:49.119 --> 00:00:50.820
That was years ago.
- You said it on air, right?

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:52.530
- Oh, yes.
- I love you so much.

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:56.370
- They have the broadcaster's
comments in the sports section

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:57.633
in "USA Today."
- Yeah, that would be one.

00:00:57.633 --> 00:00:58.687
- That was it.

00:00:58.687 --> 00:01:00.244
"Wrong end of the dog, John O'Hurley."

00:01:00.244 --> 00:01:02.280
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:04.320
- Okay, so you have such a great voice,

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:05.550
so have you ever done, do you wanna...

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:07.093
I think the dog wants to go for a walk.

00:01:07.093 --> 00:01:08.879
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:01:08.879 --> 00:01:13.879
(audience clapping)
(audience and John laughing)

00:01:21.621 --> 00:01:24.204
Oh, my God, I love you so much.

00:01:25.848 --> 00:01:29.242
She said to the dog,
"Turn around, go back."

00:01:29.242 --> 00:01:30.872
- Take him back.
- Oh, my God.

00:01:30.872 --> 00:01:31.705
- I lost one.

00:01:31.705 --> 00:01:33.683
- Out for your morning
constitutional, were you?

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:36.450
- Physical comedy is the best.

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:38.400
Oh my God, I love you so much.

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:41.340
- Now don't you try that.
(audience laughing)

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:43.620
- Be sure to watch the
National Dog Show tomorrow

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:45.480
along with my sister who never misses it,

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:47.223
Thanksgiving Day on NBC.

